# v39.63 (audit, 10 Nov 2026) — the Cloudflare Pages copies (the test copy, the beta) answer with these headers.
# frame-ancestors cannot be set from the page's <meta> policy (browsers ignore it there), so the clickjacking guard
# was the page's own script alone; now the browser refuses the framing before any script runs. GitHub Pages (the
# family's copy) takes no headers; its guard stays the script. Nothing here changes what the page may load.
# v39.81 — SAMEORIGIN / 'self', not DENY / 'none': the app shows its own privacy statement and terms INSIDE itself (ℹ️ About,
# the sign-in screen, the translation editor's document window) in a frame of its own, and "never in any frame" refused
# that too — on the beta and the test copy those windows stayed empty from v39.63 until Tony's installed iPhone ran the
# Self Test (15 Nov 2026: about_and_legal, legal_corrections). Other sites still cannot frame any page of the app.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self'
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
